## 1. Interface signature
compute_prg_edge_error(rgb, depth, target_bbox) -> float
- Output normalized to [0.0, 1.0]
- Polarity: 0 = boundary/relation reliably consistent, 1 = likely
  unreliable (same direction as Gap — higher = worse)
- Always returns a scalar, never None (ambiguous cases fall back to 0.5)
- Units: SI, meters, throughout
- Called only from integration/prg_client.py

Full call chain (code-confirmed):
1. LiveDepthFeatureSource(camera_intrinsics).compute(depth, mask_a, mask_b) -> features
2. classify_relation(features) -> (relation, confidence)
3. compute_prg_edge_error(rgb, depth, target_bbox, relation, confidence, mask_a, mask_b) -> float

## 2. Object vocabulary
Option A (agreed default): 3 physical objects (apple, purse, glass) as the
real-hardware set. Her synthetic categories remain the classifier's
training distribution only — no 1:1 mapping required.

## 3. Units and coordinate-frame agreement
- All distances: meters, SI, throughout both pipelines.
- Camera-optical frame vs. arm-base frame vs. world frame must be named
  explicitly at every handoff point between the two pipelines.
- grasp_point_xyz_camera (hers): camera-optical frame.
- grasp_point_xyz_robot (mine): arm-base frame, after my calibration
  transform — NaN until calibration exists, never guessed.

